{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques\/adjacentPairs()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"adjacentPairs","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AdjacentPairsSequence","preciseIdentifier":"s:10Algorithms21AdjacentPairsSequenceV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques\/adjacentpairs()"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:ST10AlgorithmsE13adjacentPairsAA08AdjacentC8SequenceVyxGyF::SYNTHESIZED::s:7Cliques07MaximalA0V","extendedModule":"Swift","symbolKind":"method","modules":[{"name":"Cliques","relatedModules":["Swift"]}],"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"adjacentPairs","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:10Algorithms21AdjacentPairsSequenceV","text":"AdjacentPairsSequence","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Method","role":"symbol","title":"adjacentPairs()"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Inherited from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sequence.adjacentPairs()"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"references":{"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques","url":"\/documentation\/cliques","abstract":[],"role":"collection","kind":"symbol","title":"Cliques","type":"topic"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/MaximalCliques":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MaximalCliques","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MaximalCliques","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every maximal clique of an undirected graph’s simple graph once, lazily, each in "},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order (by vertex index): an isolated vertex, or one whose only edges are loops, is a clique of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one. The order is Eppstein–Löffler–Strash’s: by the cliques’ first vertex in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"coreNumbers().degeneracyOrdering","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", then as Bron–Kerbosch with Tomita’s pivot (ties to the least"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"index) and branches in ascending index meets them. The sequence holds the graph, so iterating"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"again gives the same cliques. O(n + m) before the first clique, O(d·n·3^(d\/3)) in all for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"degeneracy d."}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","title":"MaximalCliques","type":"topic"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/MaximalCliques/adjacentPairs()":{"abstract":[],"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"adjacentPairs","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AdjacentPairsSequence","preciseIdentifier":"s:10Algorithms21AdjacentPairsSequenceV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques\/adjacentPairs()","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques\/adjacentpairs()","type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"adjacentPairs()"}}}